# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production build configuration — COMMITTED ON PURPOSE.
#
# Why this file exists
#   Vite inlines VITE_* variables at BUILD time, not at runtime. A host that
#   builds without them produces a bundle with '' compiled in, and the app then
#   reports "لم يتم ربط قاعدة البيانات" regardless of what the host dashboard
#   says afterwards. Committing them makes `npm run build` self-sufficient: any
#   host, any CI, no dashboard configuration required.
#
# Why it is safe
#   Both values are public by design. The anon key ships to every browser that
#   loads the app — it is already readable in dist/assets/*.js on the live site.
#   Every table denies it access via RLS; the app reaches data only through
#   SECURITY DEFINER RPCs. See README §3.1.
#
# ONLY public VITE_* values belong here.
#   Never add SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY or any other secret. Secrets stay in
#   .env, which is gitignored. .gitignore still blocks every other .env file;
#   this one is un-ignored explicitly.
#
# If the anon key is rotated, update this file and redeploy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://pfxkxvddashkdpzwctkm.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_3Bz-uttjgaeuqb9BzbTRJg_ksiXglZ-
